# Resizable panels
Resizable Panels divides a bounded workspace into two adjustable regions. Drag the separator or use Left/Right for side-by-side panels and Up/Down for stacked panels. Shift changes the keyboard step and Home/End jump to the configured limits.
<DocsExample title="Resizable panels" {source} {htmlSource}><Example /></DocsExample>

## Size changes and styling

`size` is the first panel's percentage. Bind it in Svelte or set the HTML element's
`size` property. `onsizechange(size)` (Svelte) and `sizechange` with
`event.detail.size` (HTML) report user-driven pointer and keyboard changes only;
programmatic assignments do not emit this event. This lets consumers remember a
preferred size without observing reflected attributes.

The HTML element exposes `::part(layout)` and `::part(handle)` for styling.
For a collapsed consumer panel, hide its disabled separator with
`aesir-resizable-panels[disabled]::part(handle) { visibility: hidden; }`.

Set `animate` to opt into a short size transition. It is off by default, bypassed
while dragging or using the keyboard separator, and disabled by reduced motion.
